.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt KVM 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kvm
.Nd the kernel virtual machine interface
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /dev/kvm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pa /dev/kvm
is Linux's KVM interface, API version 12, through which a program such as
QEMU runs virtual machines on the processor's own virtualization, Intel's
VMX or AMD's SVM.
The x86-64 kernel makes it at boot when the processor has one of them and
the firmware leaves it usable: a character device, 10:232, mode 0666.
Without either, and on the i686 kernel, there is no node.
The boot names the extension in a record,
.Ql kvm: ready: vmx
or
.Ql kvm: ready: svm .
.Pp
A program uses it through the structures and ioctls of Linux's
.In linux/kvm.h .
.Dv KVM_CREATE_VM
on
.Pa /dev/kvm
gives a descriptor of a new VM,
.Pa anon_inode:kvm-vm ,
and
.Dv KVM_CREATE_VCPU
on that a descriptor of a vCPU,
.Pa anon_inode:kvm-vcpu:N ;
both are open for reading and writing and close on exec.
A vCPU lives as long as its VM, and a VM as long as a descriptor or a
mapping of one of its vCPUs.
.Pp
Each level takes Linux's ioctls of its level:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /dev/kvm
.Dv KVM_GET_API_VERSION ,
.Dv KVM_CREATE_VM
of machine type 0,
.Dv KVM_CHECK_EXTENSION ,
.Dv KVM_GET_VCPU_MMAP_SIZE ,
.Dv KVM_GET_MSR_INDEX_LIST ,
.Dv KVM_GET_MSR_FEATURE_INDEX_LIST ,
.Dv KVM_GET_MSRS
of the feature MSRs,
.Dv KVM_GET_SUPPORTED_CPUID ,
.Dv KVM_GET_EMULATED_CPUID ,
which offers no leaf,
and
.Dv KVM_X86_GET_MCE_CAP_SUPPORTED .
.It a VM
.Dv KVM_CREATE_VCPU ,
.Dv KVM_CHECK_EXTENSION ,
.Dv KVM_SET_USER_MEMORY_REGION ,
.Dv KVM_SET_TSS_ADDR ,
.Dv KVM_SET_IDENTITY_MAP_ADDR ,
.Dv KVM_SET_NR_MMU_PAGES ,
.Dv KVM_GET_NR_MMU_PAGES ,
.Dv KVM_GET_CLOCK ,
.Dv KVM_SET_CLOCK ,
.Dv KVM_SET_BOOT_CPU_ID
and
.Dv KVM_ENABLE_CAP .
.It a vCPU
.Dv KVM_RUN ,
the registers
.Pq Dv KVM_GET_REGS , KVM_GET_SREGS , KVM_GET_FPU , KVM_GET_XSAVE , KVM_GET_XCRS , KVM_GET_DEBUGREGS
and their sets,
.Dv KVM_GET_MSRS ,
.Dv KVM_SET_MSRS ,
.Dv KVM_SET_CPUID2 ,
.Dv KVM_GET_CPUID2 ,
.Dv KVM_GET_VCPU_EVENTS ,
.Dv KVM_SET_VCPU_EVENTS ,
.Dv KVM_GET_MP_STATE ,
.Dv KVM_SET_MP_STATE ,
.Dv KVM_INTERRUPT ,
.Dv KVM_NMI ,
.Dv KVM_SET_SIGNAL_MASK ,
.Dv KVM_SET_GUEST_DEBUG ,
.Dv KVM_X86_SETUP_MCE
and
.Dv KVM_X86_SET_MCE .
.El
.Pp
.Dv KVM_CHECK_EXTENSION
answers 1, or a count, for each capability the kernel makes true, and 0
for the rest.
A capability turns on with the part of the kernel that gives it: those of
the memory slots, the in-kernel interrupt controller and ioeventfds are
not given yet, and neither is any that depends on the backend.
.Pp
A vCPU's descriptor maps
.Dv KVM_GET_VCPU_MMAP_SIZE
bytes, two pages: the
.Vt struct kvm_run
page and the page port I/O data goes through, at
.Dv KVM_PIO_PAGE_OFFSET .
A shared mapping is the kernel's own pages, which
.Dv KVM_RUN
reads and writes, and a fork's child shares it.
A private mapping gives each page as it was when first touched, as a
private mapping of a file does, and its writes stay its own.
A page past the two raises
.Dv SIGBUS .
.Pp
A VM belongs to the address space that made it.
Its ioctls, and those of its vCPUs, made from another, as a fork's child
would make them, fail with
.Er EIO .
.Pp
.Dv KVM_RUN
gives the guest the answer to the last exit's port or MMIO read first,
then returns
.Er EINTR
at once when
.Va immediate_exit
is set in the run page, and also when a signal is pending or another
thread asked the vCPU to stop, with
.Dv KVM_EXIT_INTR
in
.Va exit_reason .
That
.Er EINTR
is never restarted, with or without
.Dv SA_RESTART ,
as on Linux.
The backends that run guests are not in this kernel yet:
.Dv KVM_RUN
otherwise fails with
.Er EOPNOTSUPP .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /dev/kvm
.It Pa /dev/kvm
the interface
.El
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er ENOTTY
An ioctl that
.Pa /dev/kvm
or a VM does not take.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
An ioctl that a vCPU does not take; an argument outside Linux's bounds,
such as a machine type other than 0, a vCPU id of 256 or more, a TSS past
4 GiB less three pages, register state the processor would refuse, an
XSAVE image past the guest's XCR0, or a flag Linux does not define.
.It Bq Er E2BIG
A list longer than the call takes, more than 256 CPUID entries or 256
MSRs or more; or a buffer too small for the list asked for, whose count
.Dv KVM_GET_MSR_INDEX_LIST
and
.Dv KVM_GET_MSR_FEATURE_INDEX_LIST
then write back.
.It Bq Er EEXIST
.Dv KVM_CREATE_VCPU
of an id the VM has.
.It Bq Er EBUSY
.Dv KVM_SET_IDENTITY_MAP_ADDR
or
.Dv KVM_SET_BOOT_CPU_ID
once the VM has a vCPU;
.Dv KVM_SET_GUEST_DEBUG
while an exception waits.
.It Bq Er ENXIO
.Dv KVM_INTERRUPT
while an interrupt waits.
.It Bq Er EIO
An ioctl from an address space other than the VM's.
.It Bq Er EINTR
.Dv KVM_RUN
ended by
.Va immediate_exit ,
a signal or a request to stop.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
.Dv KVM_RUN ,
until the backends run guests.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ioctl 2 ,
.Xr mmap 2 ,
.Xr limits 7
.Sh STANDARDS
Linux's KVM API, version 12, for x86, as its
.Pa Documentation/virt/kvm/api.rst
gives it.
.Sh BUGS
At most 64 vCPUs in a VM, with ids below 256, and 256 memory slots.
No in-kernel PIC, IOAPIC or PIT, no coalesced MMIO, no dirty ring, no SMM
and no nested virtualization.
